      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFlashInfer's `trtllm_batch_decode_with_kv_cache` and `trtllm_batch_context_with_kv_cache` allocate and zero a fresh multi-CTA-KV counter buffer on every call when `multi_ctas_kv_counter_buffer` is not passed (`_resolve_trtllm_gen_multi_ctas_kv_counter_buffer` in flashinfer 0.7.0). With trtllm-gen, this adds a fill kernel before every FMHA call, in every full-attention layer, every step, and the fill is also captured into the CUDA graphs. The kernel resets the counters at the end of each launch, so one zeroed buffer can be reused.\n\nThis PR makes the FlashInfer MHA backend own one persistent counter buffer and pass it to both trtllm-gen entry points. The buffer is sized once for the worst-case batch (`max_num_batched_tokens` × query heads; DCP decode all-gathers heads), so it never grows after graph capture. The FlashInfer MLA backend already does this (`_get_multi_ctas_kv_counter_buffer` in `flashinfer_mla.py`). The same fix was made in SGLang (sgl-project/sglang#33063).\n\nFLASHINFER is the default backend for non-MLA causal models on SM10x (B200/GB200/B300/GB300), so this path is hit by default there. XQA (SM90) doesn't use the counter and is unchanged.\n\n**Duplicate check:** I searched open vLLM PRs for `multi_ctas_kv_counter_buffer`, \"trtllm decode counter buffer\" and \"flashinfer trtllm MHA workspace\". No open PR covers the MHA path.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```bash\nPATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/v1/attention/test_trtllm_attention_integration.py \\\n  tests/v1/attention/test_attention_backends.py -q -k \"trtllm or flashinfer or FLASHINFER\"\n```\n\n`FlashInferImpl` is constructed under `set_current_vllm_config` in the integration test, so these tests exercise the new buffer on the trtllm-gen path.\n\nBenchmark: `vllm bench latency --model Qwen/Qwen3-8B --attention-backend FLASHINFER --input-len 1024 --output-len 128 --num-iters-warmup 3 --num-iters 10`, on 1x GB300 (sm103, decode_backend=trtllm-gen). Three alternating runs each.\n\n## Test Result\n\n- Tests: 42 passed, 2 skipped.\n- Latency (avg over 10 iterations per run):\n\n| batch | main (3 runs) | this PR (3 runs) | change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0.4872 / 0.4842 / 0.4855 s | 0.4781 / 0.4783 / 0.4783 s | -1.5% |\n| 64 | 1.2646 / 1.2670 / 1.2649 s | 1.2744 / 1.2659 / 1.2679 s | within noise |\n\nAt batch 1 this saves about 58 µs per decode step (36 layers).\n\nNo accuracy eval: the change only affects which zeroed scratch buffer the kernel uses, and the kernel outputs are unchanged.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to write this change and run the tests and benchmarks above. Draft until the submitter has reviewed every changed line.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
